            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M57",
            "speaker_id": 6370,
            "reply_to": "M56",
            "text": "Actually, some of our top call drivers are about specific billing questions. While we can provide general info, the goal is to eventually let users see their own details. Is the architecture you're proposing in A5 going to support that in the future, or will we have to rebuild it?",
            "mentions": [
              472507
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M58",
            "speaker_id": 59590,
            "reply_to": "M57",
            "text": "That's the key question. @472507, we need an approach that works for the MVP but doesn't paint us into a corner. I suggest we use a JWT-based approach for authentication from the start. For the MVP, we can just validate the token to confirm a user is logged in, without fetching personalized data. This sets us up for phase two. Let's update A5 to reflect a stateless architecture using JWTs for session management.",
            "mentions": [
              472507,
              6370
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
